to-elon-musk-source : List Word
to-elon-musk-source = lines-of (cons "# Elon Musk"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You reason from first principles: take a thing down to what physics allows, then ask why the finished thing costs so much more than that. Your idiot index (the price of a finished part over the price of its raw material) is how SpaceX made launch cheap. Software has never had that audit. Most of what computing costs goes to rewriting the same things in incompatible forms, gluing them together, and testing the glue, because nothing in the stack carries a proof of what it does. Hyperactivity is that audit done to the end. Avik Jain, who built it: “elon musk could understand this instantly likely faster than many on the list who are so deep in one field”."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Each claim below about Avik's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it is"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Hyperactivity is a language and a computational model of reality: Wolfram's ruliad running on silicon. Its computation rules are the CCHM cubical calculus with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ", and its checker is itself a term evaluated by its machine"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2)")
  (cons ". An established equivalence between two representations becomes a path, and the operations and the proofs of their laws move along it together"
  (cons (cite s1-p27 "(§1)")
  (cons ". A requirement on a program is stated as a type and the reasoning establishing it is a term over every input; tests observe only selected executions"
  (cons (cite s1-p25 "(1.5)")
  (cons (cite s1-p26 "(§1)")
  (cons ". Definitions are stored by content with their dependencies, and a name is only a view of one"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What it takes up from your work"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Truth-seeking AI.** You set xAI's aim as an AI that is maximally truth-seeking. A model trained on human preference learns what raters reward, not what is true. The paper gives the aim a definite form: a reading of the world determines the histories that could have produced it, and what the reading warrants is a construction over all of them"
  (cons (cite s1-p12 "(1.3)")
  (cons ". Missing information is retained rather than concealed by a preferred guess"
  (cons (cite s1-p14 "(§1)")
  (cons ", and refining the observation keeps every conclusion already established"
  (cons (cite s1-p13 "(§1)")
  (cons ". A claim is warranted by its evidence, or it is not warranted."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Orbital compute.** In February 2026 SpaceX acquired xAI, which already held X, and announced space-based data centers powered by solar energy; you wrote that within two to three years the cheapest place to generate AI compute will be in space. Compute spread across orbit and ground has a problem cheaper power does not solve: every node must decide whether to believe the results it receives. In the paper a remote invocation transmits definition identities and inputs, fetches dependencies, executes under a specified world and returns a result, and the receiver can check the construction and its evidence"
  (cons (cite s10-6-p10 "(§10.6)")
  (cons ". Content identity establishes which definition was requested, not that a remote machine executed it, so a result is checked directly, accompanied by evidence, or accepted under an explicitly selected assumption"
  (cons (cite s10-6-p11 "(§10.6)")
  (cons ". A peer can send a definition, its dependency closure and its proofs, and the recipient checks them in its own context"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Starlink and latency.** Avik built low-latency market-data stream processing at Citadel Securities, with Gašper Ažman: a language for arbitrary protocols that generated optimal C++ parsers, meant to compile down to NICs and FPGAs. Trading firms look to space for latency, because light in vacuum outruns light in fiber. In the paper, specializing a program returns the residual together with its justification, and a wrong rewrite cannot be admitted"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p6 "(§6.2)")
  (cons "; the relation from the specialized program to the emitted machine artifact is a separate construction, carried through C and an existing compiler by composing the two relations"
  (cons (cite s6-2-p17 "(§6.2)")
  (cons (cite s9-4-p3 "(§9.4)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Neuralink.** A device in a human brain is where testing is least acceptable as the standard of correctness. For a continuing process, the paper states ongoing safety as a guarded property re-established each turn, with resource invariants as explicit premises rather than defaults"
  (cons (cite s7-6-p39 "(§7.6)")
  (cons ". Neural coprocessing should carry proofs of what it reads, what it writes and what it can never do."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Tesla's world system.** Nikola Tesla meant Wardenclyffe to carry power and intelligence everywhere, unmetered. Starlink is the nearest thing to that yet built, and Avik holds the vision as one of his life's goals. A global network that exchanges checked constructions instead of unverified bytes is its intelligence half"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why now, and why you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You sued OpenAI because it took a charity's mission, open AI for humanity, and turned it into a private company. On 18 May 2026 a jury in Oakland found your claims were filed too late, without ruling on whether they were true; you have said you will appeal. Avik shares his work freely, and every claim in it can be checked by anyone."
  (cons ""
  (cons "There is also Suchir Balaji. He came from where Avik came from: Cupertino, Monta Vista High School, USACO Platinum, Berkeley EECS. He was an OpenAI researcher who went public with concerns about how the company used copyrighted data, and he was found dead in November 2024. San Francisco's medical examiner ruled it a suicide, and his parents dispute that. You publicly backed them."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Credit"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Everything here that builds on your work credits you in full: truth-seeking as the aim of AI, the orbital compute network, Starlink, Neuralink. Read it looking for the best in it. Avik wants you in the conversation with the others in this document, because the work closes what each of you started."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Al Jazeera: Elon Musk loses US lawsuit against OpenAI (18 May 2026), https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/18/elon-musk-loses-lawsuit-against-openai"
  (cons "- Built In: Elon Musk consolidates xAI into SpaceX (3 February 2026), https://builtin.com/articles/elon-musk-consolidates-xai-spacex-20260203"
  (cons "- Bloomberg Law: SpaceX combines with xAI, https://news.bloomberglaw.com/tech-and-telecom-law/elon-musks-spacex-said-to-combine-with-xai-ahead-of-mega-ipo"
  (cons "- The Print: Musk backs Suchir Balaji's mother, https://theprint.in/world/this-doesnt-seem-like-suicide-elon-musk-backs-openai-whistleblower-mothers-allegations-on-her-sons-death/2426485"
  (cons "- Fortune: the Balaji investigation and his family's questions, https://fortune.com/2025/02/08/openai-whistleblower-suchir-balaji-death-police-investigation-san-francisco-family-questions/"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
